DOS-PORT (patch 0098, Phase 9 wave 23 W23B). Default-flips the
SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_TILEMAP_CACHE killswitch from ON to OFF after
W23A real-HW measurement found the wave-23 W23A Path B tilemap
cache is a NET REGRESSION on real HW. Mimiga heavy-music gameplay
+11.23 ms vs wave-22 W22.5 baseline per docs/PHASE11-WAVE-23-
FINDINGS.md sec. 11. Cache architecture + 13-counter instrumentation
+ kbd diagnostic + adaptive-alpha state machine all PRESERVED intact
for wave-24 architectural redesign.

Mechanism of the regression (per flush-instr's findings sec. 11):
  - Cache miss path costs ~2x uncached render: render-INTO-cache
    AND blit-cache-TO-window are BOTH bandwidth-bound on PODP83's
    17 MB/s memcpy throughput.
  - Break-even hit rate is 92% (cache must hit 92% of frames to
    match uncached cost).
  - Real-HW gameplay aggregate hit rate is 44.7% (well below
    break-even).
  - Adaptive-alpha has two blind spots that prevented the fail-safe
    from triggering: (a) hit-cost not measured-derived, only
    threshold-compared, so high-cost hits don't disable cache; and
    (b) thrash detection requires 10 consecutive LOW-cost misses
    but real-HW misses are HIGH-cost so adaptive-alpha never disabled
    the cache despite the regression.

Patch 0098 ONLY flips the default. ~5 LOC change in
`_abl_tilemap_cache_killswitch()`:

  Before (patch 0097):
    static const bool v = _strict_falsy_env("SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_TILEMAP_CACHE");
  After (patch 0098):
    static const bool v = !_strict_truthy_env("SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_TILEMAP_CACHE");

Semantics flip:
  - Before: env unset -> killswitch INACTIVE -> cache ENABLED (default ON)
  - After:  env unset -> killswitch ACTIVE   -> cache DISABLED (default OFF)
  - env "1" enables cache (opt-in for ablation iters)
  - env "0" / empty / anything else: cache stays DISABLED

The `_strict_falsy_env` helper from patch 0097 stays in tree but is
unused after this flip -- kept for symmetry with `_strict_truthy_env`
and for any future opt-OUT semantics. Future-cleanup task: remove
`_strict_falsy_env` if it remains unused after wave-24 redesign.

Why this restoration is safe:
  - When killswitch is ACTIVE (default), `map_draw()` falls through
    to `_tilemap_render_uncached_full_loop()` -- byte-identical to
    pre-patch-0097 map_draw body. Counter increments NOT made (per
    W23A contract sec. 3.2). Mode_draw_scene cost matches W22.5
    baseline.
  - Counter emission (gated on MODE_DRAW_SCENE_INSTR=1, NOT the
    killswitch) still fires when MODE_DRAW_SCENE_INSTR=1 is set.
    The post-build-qa-smoke-C fix in patch 0097 sec. 9.b ensures
    `bg_state=D fg_state=D` from block 1 under killswitch -- so
    flush-instr's analysis tooling correctly identifies "wave-23
    cache disabled" runs vs adaptive-alpha-disabled runs.
  - Cache architecture + adaptive-alpha + 13-counter storage remain
    intact for wave-24 redesign. Re-enabling per-iter for cache-
    on ablation is just `SET SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_TILEMAP_CACHE=1`.

What stays preserved (NOT removed):
  - `Renderer::drawCachedTilemap()` + `Tileset::drawTileToSurface()`
  - Cache surfaces + cache key tuple + lazy-alloc + reset hook
  - Adaptive-alpha state machine (8.6 ms BG / 15.4 ms FG thresholds)
  - 13-field `[mds-tilemap-cache ...]` instrumentation line
  - 5-field kbd diagnostic appendage to kbd/audio block log
  - Tile mutation counter
  - All NXE::Diag accessors + file-top + end-of-file wrappers
  - `_strict_falsy_env()` helper (unused but retained)

Documentation:
  - docs/BOOT.md: TILEMAP_CACHE entry rewritten -- reframed as opt-IN
    via "1" (was opt-OUT via "0"). Default-OFF rationale + W23A
    regression measurement cited. Wave-24 redesign noted.
  - BOOT.md gitignored per pre-existing convention; on-disk only.

Test plan (subsequent tasks per team-lead's W23B brief):
  - DOSBox-X smoke gate (build-qa): cache-disabled-default produces
    same fps as wave-22 W22.5 baseline.
    - Smoke A: env-unset baseline. NO `[mds-tilemap-cache]` lines
      emit (instrumentation off); cache also OFF; mds_tilemap_bg +
      mds_tilemap_fg match W22.5 numbers.
    - Smoke B: MODE_DRAW_SCENE_INSTR=1 only (other env unset).
      `[mds-tilemap-cache]` lines emit with `bg_state=D fg_state=D`
      from block 1 + `bg_h=0 bg_m=0 fg_h=0 fg_m=0` (confirms
      default-disabled). mds_tilemap_bg + mds_tilemap_fg match
      W22.5 baseline.
    - Smoke C: MODE_DRAW_SCENE_INSTR=1 + TILEMAP_CACHE=1 (opt-in
      cache enabled). `[mds-tilemap-cache]` lines emit with
      `bg_state=E fg_state=E` from block 1 (cache active). Smoke
      reproduces the wave-23 W23A behavior pre-default-flip.
  - Real-HW iter (realhw): W23B short cycle. Cache disabled
    default. Mimiga heavy-music mean flip-total returns to
    ~31 ms (wave-22 W22.5 baseline) confirming the regression
    is gone.
  - Findings (flush-instr): brief findings sec. 13 confirming
    baseline restoration. No new architecture authored in W23B;
    that's wave-24 scope.

Reviewer ack:
  - team-lead: directly approved option 1 default-flip per
    flush-instr's W23A sec. 12 verdict (2026-05-05 user direction).
  - flush-instr: not re-reviewed for this micro-patch -- the change
    is a single-line semantic flip + BOOT.md update; no contract
    deviation.
  - sdl-engine: not re-reviewed -- kbd diagnostic unchanged.
  - build-qa: smoke gate per the test plan above is the next gate.

Patch slot 0098 used for this regression mitigation per team-lead's
W23B brief. Slot 0098 was originally reserved for hand-rolled
`_blit_indexed` optimization (wave-23 design Q5); that work moves
to slot 0099+ if wave-24 redesign retains the cache concept.

